     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Good Point Chris. I made that to make sure that after filtering the first row of a matrix, it is still a matrix. Because when I did some testing using REPORT() it appears as a vector. Am I wrong?. <br><br>I know how to code it in R:<br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">a1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> numeric</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">a1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model_data$Z</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,]%*%(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">model_data$U</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,]))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Quick result in R</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>     </span><span style=\"color:#660\">[,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,]</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">19</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">a1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model_data$Z</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">drop </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> F</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]%*%</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">model_data$U</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> drop </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">F</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># How I think c++ would work</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>     </span><span style=\"color:#660\">[,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,]</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">19</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><div><br>But I don&#39;t know how to perform it in template/C++;</div></div>"
