     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">One important thing to note is that an Eigen matmult operation is significantly faster than the cwise -&gt; sum alternative. In high dimensional cases you would definitely want to use matmult.</blockquote></div></blockquote></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>In the simple example shown below where a 1e4 x 1e4 dimensional matrix is multiplied by a 1e4 dimensional vector the cwise -&gt; sum equivalent was around 7 times slower. The explicit cwise operation was faster than the array casting method, which seems to have additional overhead.  Note, the discrepancies increase with the object dimensions. </div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><div><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\tauto t1 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\tY_i = X_ij * B_j;\r\n\tauto t2 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\tauto time_matmult = std::chrono::duration_cast&lt;std::chrono::milliseconds&gt;( t2 - t1 ).count();\r\n\t\r\n\tauto t3 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\tfor (int i=0; i&lt;I; i++) {\r\n\t\t\tY_i(i) = (X_ij.row(i).array() * Btrans_j.array()).sum();\r\n\t}\r\n\tauto t4 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\tauto time_cwise1 = std::chrono::duration_cast&lt;std::chrono::milliseconds&gt;( t4 - t3 ).count();\r\n\t\r\n\tauto t5 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\tfor (int i=0; i&lt;I; i++) {\r\n\t\t\tY_i(i) = (X_ij.row(i).cwiseProduct(Btrans_j)).sum();\r\n\t}\r\n\tauto t6 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\tauto time_cwise2 = std::chrono::duration_cast&lt;std::chrono::milliseconds&gt;( t6 - t5 ).count();<br><br></span><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></div><div style=\"border-width:1px;border-style:solid;border-color:rgb(187,187,187);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><code><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><div>time_matmult: 1106 milliseconds</div><div>time_cwise1: 7158 <span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">milliseconds</span></div><div>time_cwise2: 6608 <span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">milliseconds</span></div></span></div></code></div></div></div></code></div></div></div>"
